   1: You are working in the GRIOT repository.
   2: 
   3: Your task is to design and implement the complete UI system, top to bottom, for GRIOT: a mobile-first, local-first learning shell that begins like a notes app and gradually reveals itself as an evidence-aware, agent-assisted mastery environment.
   4: 
   5: Do not perform a visual reskin only. Build a coherent system of screens, components, presentation models, navigation states, interaction rules, settings, and workflows that makes the existing domain capabilities understandable to a person who initially thinks they are using a notes app.
   6: 
   7: Read these files before changing code:
   8: - docs/architecture.md
   9: - docs/goal-architect-implementation-plan.md
  10: - newui.txt
  11: - Existing controller, presenters, workflow modules, UI screens, theme settings, font gateway, command registry, research workflow, mission workflow, review workflow, operation workflow, and tests.
