 250: 2. First capture:
 251:    - Support quick note, question, URL/source, pasted text, and project idea.
 252:    - Explain where the item was saved.
 253:    - Show only 2–3 contextual next actions.
 254:    - Do not show every available power tool.
 255: 
 256: 3. First next action:
 257:    - For a note:
 258:      - Explain this.
 259:      - Find prerequisites.
 260:      - Attach to a goal.
 261:    - For a source:
 262:      - Extract key ideas.
 263:      - Assess source.
 264:      - Make practice questions.
 265:    - For a question:
 266:      - Research it.
 267:      - Turn it into an experiment.
 268:      - Add supporting notes.
 269:    - For an experiment:
 270:      - Add measurement.
 271:      - Find prerequisites.
 272:      - Create a next task.
 273: 
 274: 4. Goal architect:
 275:    - Keep existing goal architect design and implementation direction.
 276:    - It must remain a focused bottom sheet or contained flow, never a permanent general chat screen.
 277:    - Ask one high-leverage question at a time.
 278:    - Show rationale for the question.
 279:    - Preserve skipped answers.
 280:    - Build a transparent working map.
 281:    - Label model contribution “Agent hypothesis — verify or edit.”
 282:    - Allow fully manual use without an API key.
 283:    - Offer web research only after explicit opt-in.
 284:    - Create mission cards only after the user approves a clearly labeled draft.
