 286: ==================================================
 287: FIELD: MAIN CANVAS
 288: ==================================================
 289: 
 290: FIELD is the primary home and replaces the feeling of a generic list of notes.
 291: 
 292: It must still use the existing card and group model. Do not build a separate graph database or duplicate source of truth.
 293: 
 294: FIELD presents a bounded, scrollable working set:
 295: - Current group / workspace context.
 296: - Mission module only when a mission exists.
 297: - Current next action.
 298: - Notes, questions, sources, concepts, claims, experiments, tasks, and results represented as cards.
 299: - Cards remain the actual domain cards.
 300: - Filters are presentation state, not destructive reclassification.
 301: 
 302: Card visual grammar:
 303: - Semantic role label.
 304: - Title.
 305: - Concise preview.
 306: - Relevant status only: due, source retained, evidence caution, agent-generated, selected, incomplete, blocked.
 307: - Provenance affordance when provenance exists.
 308: - One primary contextual action available on expansion.
 309: - Selection affordance is always visible and accessible.
 310: - Cards must remain easy to scan one-handed.
 311: 
 312: Card roles:
 313: - Note: user capture or working thought.
 314: - Source: imported/pasted/retained source.
 315: - Chunk: readable extracted learning material.
 316: - Question: unresolved or recall prompt.
 317: - Concept: a structured explanation/idea.
 318: - Claim: a proposition supported or needing support.
 319: - Experiment: hypothesis, method, measure, result, next action.
 320: - Task: a concrete action.
 321: - Deliverable: output that demonstrates capability.
 322: - Group: scope/container/document/milestone.
 323: - Goal: workspace mission.
 324: 
 325: Mission module:
 326: - Only shown for workspaces with a mission.
 327: - Display:
 328:   - Goal title.
 329:   - Target deliverable.
 330:   - One success criterion.
 331:   - Counts: blockers, prerequisites, evidence, next tasks.
 332:   - One recommended next action with a short deterministic reason.
 333: - Tapping it opens the status gap report.
 334: - Never show an opaque “percent complete.”
 335: - If any maturity indicator exists, it must state that it is heuristic and explain why.
 336: 
 337: Status gap report:
 338: - Answer:
 339:   - What do I want?
 340:   - What do I have?
 341:   - What is missing?
 342:   - What should I do next?
 343: - Use deterministic card graph analysis before any model enrichment.
 344: - Clearly distinguish:
 345:   - Deterministic result.
 346:   - Agent hypothesis.
 347:   - Web-grounded evidence.
 348: - Allow the user to turn a recommendation into a task, research preflight, experiment draft, or study action.
