 433: ==================================================
 434: AGENT SYSTEM
 435: ==================================================
 436: 
 437: Agents are user-configurable, scoped tools.
 438: 
 439: Do not use a single global “AI” assistant with a hidden prompt.
 440: 
 441: Build an Agent Studio with:
 442: - Built-in agents.
 443: - User-created agents.
 444: - Session-only agents.
 445: - Workspace-bound agents.
 446: - Global saved agents.
 447: - Duplicate built-in agent to customize.
 448: - Export/import agent definition as JSON only if safe and compatible with existing storage patterns.
 449: 
 450: Required built-in agents:
 451: 1. Goal Architect:
 452:    - Clarifies intention.
 453:    - Builds working map.
 454:    - Proposes mission draft.
 455:    - May propose research queries.
 456:    - Does not browse without approval.
 457: 
 458: 2. Learning Coach:
 459:    - Explains selected material.
 460:    - Finds misconceptions.
 461:    - Creates teaching explanations.
 462:    - Generates questions only from available context.
 463:    - Encourages prediction and application rather than long lectures.
 464: 
 465: 3. Research Scout:
 466:    - Proposes/refines research queries.
 467:    - Classifies source needs.
 468:    - Helps assess retained evidence.
 469:    - Uses actual web results only after SearchGateway runs.
 470:    - Never claims it searched unless a search receipt proves it.
 471: 
 472: 4. Prerequisite Mapper:
 473:    - Identifies missing concepts and dependencies.
 474:    - Outputs explicit question/concept cards.
 475:    - Marks uncertain suggestions as hypotheses.
 476: 
 477: 5. Experiment Designer:
 478:    - Converts an uncertainty into:
 479:      - Hypothesis.
 480:      - Method.
 481:      - Required tools/materials.
 482:      - Measurement.
 483:      - Expected result.
 484:      - Stop condition.
 485:      - Next action.
 486:    - Never claims an experiment was conducted.
 487: 
 488: 6. Study Builder:
 489:    - Converts selected learner-approved content into recall or cloze material.
 490:    - Requires explicit confirmation before enrollment in FSRS/review.
 491:    - Must preserve links to source content.
 492: 
 493: 7. Capstone Planner:
 494:    - Turns a mission and selected evidence into milestones, tasks, deliverables, and explicit unknowns.
 495:    - Must avoid creating false certainty or arbitrary deadlines.
 496: 
 497: Agent definition model:
 498: Create or extend a serializable domain model, preferably in entities, such as:
 499: 
 500: type AgentProfile = {
 501:   id: string;
 502:   name: string;
 503:   description: string;
 504:   scope: "builtin" | "global" | "workspace" | "session";
 505:   systemPrompt: string;
 506:   allowedCapabilities: AgentCapability[];
 507:   defaultModelId?: string;
 508:   preferredOutputRoles: SemanticRole[];
 509:   contextPolicy: ContextPolicy;
 510:   webPolicy: "never" | "preflight-required";
 511:   outputPolicy: OutputPolicy;
 512:   createdAt: number;
 513:   updatedAt: number;
 514:   isBuiltin: boolean;
 515:   isEditable: boolean;
 516:   sourceProfileId?: string;
 517: };
 518: 
 519: type AgentCapability =
 520:   | "explain"
 521:   | "goal-architect"
 522:   | "query-planning"
 523:   | "research-synthesis"
 524:   | "prerequisite-mapping"
 525:   | "experiment-planning"
 526:   | "study-generation"
 527:   | "capstone-planning"
 528:   | "custom";
 529: 
 530: type ContextPolicy = {
 531:   defaultScope: "selected-only" | "bounded-workspace" | "mission-only";
 532:   maxCards: number;
 533:   maxCharacters: number;
 534:   allowSources: boolean;
 535:   allowMission: boolean;
 536:   allowPriorOutputs: boolean;
 537: };
 538: 
 539: type OutputPolicy = {
 540:   allowCardCreation: boolean;
 541:   allowedRoles: SemanticRole[];
 542:   requireReviewBeforeSave: boolean;
 543:   createGroupForOutputs: boolean;
 544: };
 545: 
 546: Requirements:
 547: - Built-ins are read-only.
 548: - “Customize” duplicates a built-in agent into a user-owned profile.
 549: - User edits never mutate built-ins.
 550: - Every prompt is visible and editable in the agent editor.
 551: - Explain the impact of each capability and policy in plain language.
 552: - Validate prompt, name, capability, model selection, and context limits.
 553: - Do not allow profiles to request unbounded workspace upload.
 554: - Allow session-only changes that disappear after the session.
 555: - Persist global and workspace-scoped profiles safely.
 556: - Keep existing assistant profiles backwards compatible through migration/adapters.
 557: - If a profile references a missing model, show an actionable fallback selector; never silently switch models.
 558: 
 559: Agent Studio UI:
 560: - List agents by scope: Built-in, Workspace, My agents, Session.
 561: - Each item displays:
 562:   - Name.
 563:   - What it does.
 564:   - Web availability.
 565:   - Default context policy.
 566:   - Default model if assigned.
 567:   - Editable / built-in state.
 568: - Agent detail:
 569:   - Purpose.
 570:   - Prompt editor.
 571:   - Allowed actions.
 572:   - Context policy.
 573:   - Web policy.
 574:   - Output behavior.
 575:   - Model selection.
 576:   - Test with sample context only if test execution is truthfully scoped and clearly separate from saved actions.
 577: - Prompt editor must not expose users to opaque raw system behavior only:
 578:   - Provide a plain-language “Behavior” summary.
 579:   - Provide the exact editable prompt.
 580:   - Provide a “Prompt Architect” action that proposes a revised prompt but never overwrites without confirmation.
 581:   - Show diff before applying a generated prompt revision.
 582:   - Preserve version history or at minimum a recoverable previous version for the latest edit.
 583: - Do not send prompts or cards to a model merely by opening the editor.
 584: 
 585: Prompt Architect:
 586: - This is an optional agent-assisted tool for designing another agent profile.
 587: - Inputs:
 588:   - User goal.
 589:   - Desired behavior.
 590:   - Expected inputs.
 591:   - Desired outputs.
 592:   - Boundaries.
 593:   - Tone.
 594:   - Model/capabilities available.
 595: - Output:
 596:   - Proposed name.
 597:   - Description.
 598:   - System prompt.
 599:   - Context policy.
 600:   - Suggested output roles.
 601:   - Suggested web policy.
 602:   - Safety/quality rationale.
 603: - Must open an AI preflight showing what will be sent.
 604: - Must show a diff.
 605: - Must require explicit save.
 606: - Must store provenance that an agent designed/revised the profile, with model metadata.
 607: - Must not grant web access or broad context automatically.
 608: 
 609: ==================================================
 610: CUSTOM COMMAND SYSTEM
 611: ==================================================
 612: 
 613: Custom commands are first-class user tools, not a hidden advanced setting.
 614: 
 615: Preserve existing command definitions and pipeline behavior.
 616: 
 617: Create Command Workshop.
 618: 
 619: A custom command may be:
 620: - Deterministic macro: a saved ordered pipeline of existing deterministic commands.
 621: - Agent command: a named agent profile plus explicit input/output policy.
 622: - Guided action: a preflight-backed shortcut that opens a known operation with defaults.
 623: - Research command: an explicit research workflow shortcut that always requires web preflight.
 624: - Hybrid pipeline: deterministic stages plus a declared agent stage and/or research stage.
 625: 
 626: Do not allow arbitrary hidden code execution.
 627: 
 628: Custom command definition model should include:
 629: - id.
 630: - name.
 631: - aliases.
 632: - plain-language label.
 633: - description.
 634: - kind.
 635: - pipeline expression or stage list.
 636: - agentProfileId when applicable.
 637: - required input roles/count.
 638: - allowed input scope.
 639: - web use declaration.
 640: - output roles.
 641: - destination policy.
 642: - whether preflight is mandatory.
 643: - session/workspace/global scope.
 644: - createdAt/updatedAt.
 645: - version/source metadata.
 646: - optional icon only if it remains accessible and not essential to meaning.
 647: 
 648: Command workshop UI:
 649: - Start with templates:
 650:   - Explain simply.
 651:   - Challenge my reasoning.
 652:   - Turn notes into a practice set.
 653:   - Research and compare sources.
 654:   - Design an experiment.
 655:   - Build a capstone plan.
 656:   - My custom pipeline.
 657: - Command composer:
 658:   - Name and plain language description.
 659:   - Input requirements.
 660:   - Stage builder with reorderable stages.
 661:   - Context selector.
 662:   - Agent selector if applicable.
 663:   - Model selection if applicable.
 664:   - Web disclosure if applicable.
 665:   - Output card roles.
 666:   - Destination.
 667:   - Preflight preview.
 668:   - Underlying pipeline expression.
 669: - Every stage must display:
 670:   - What it reads.
 671:   - Whether it uses model/web.
 672:   - What it creates.
 673:   - Side effects.
 674: - Command validation:
 675:   - Detect empty commands.
 676:   - Reject invalid stage combinations.
 677:   - Reject non-existent agent profile.
 678:   - Reject required-selection commands when no selection exists.
 679:   - Reject web usage without explicit preflight.
 680:   - Reject output role conflicts.
 681:   - Reject pipeline stages that cannot consume the previous stage’s outputs, where type knowledge exists.
 682: - Commands can be pinned to the Tool Deck.
 683: - Commands can be duplicated and edited.
 684: - Built-in commands remain available and cannot be corrupted by user edits.
 685: - Existing typed command aliases must continue working.
 686: - If custom command behavior cannot be fully inferred, describe exposure conservatively rather than claiming it is deterministic, AI-free, or web-free.
